Z||000000||Haze_Performance||11-27-2001||10:54 AM||||I tried a search... no luck..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I'm looking for pics of Black 1988 GT's with beechwood interior. (with both Gold & Black stock wheels)<P>I'm thinking of selling off all my Fieros & picking one up, but I need a little visual stimulation...<P>Greatly appreciate any help you can give me..<P><BR>Thank You<BR>-Haze  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">    <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="purple">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000001||Nashco||11-27-2001||12:33 PM||||I don't have the best of pics, but it's a start and it'll bump it to the top <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/jbnash/myfiero.jpg"> <P>I just got new wheels, but this is a better shot of contrasting interior/exterior:<P> <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/jbnash/fiero/fullwheels.jpg"> <P>I love the beachwood interior color, and along with the gold wheels and black car, it's a great contrast.  I liked the color choice even more in person than in pictures (I bought it on ebay).  I hate the pinstripes on my car, but that's not too bad to deal with <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Excellent choice in my opinion, but whatever you want to do is what's best!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
