Z||000003||Cheever3000||11-27-2001||01:29 PM||||My interior before short-shifter...<BR>===================================<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GT_int_1_1.jpg"> <BR>===================================<BR>Another...<BR>===================================<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GT_int_2_1.jpg"> <BR>===================================<BR>As is sits now.  I don't like bras, but the wreck no longer allows a perfect fit of the facia, so it's better than without it.<BR>===================================<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GT_in_driveway_1.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cheever_gold_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||11-27-2001||03:37 PM||||Go for it!  The <B>BEST</B> color combo on '88 GT's is the black on gold with tan interior.  I have owned 3 identical GT's like this and have loved all of them more than any of the other Fieros I have had over the years.<P>My "baby" is a black 16K nile '88 GT with soon to have tan leather interior and gold wheels.  They look absolutely beautiful when cleaned/waxed, but you will have to be more dilligent with the cleaning than  before....they look awful when dirty (and they get dirty fast).<P>I wish I was at my other computer.....I would send you a bunch of pics of my GT.  I would suggest buying a low mileage one though.  Beechwood interior parts and nice gold wheels are very difficult to find and even harder to find in "mint" shape, so buying a lower  mileage one will give you a better base to start from.  <P>Good luck and again.....GO FOR IT!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||10
